{
  "_what": "The kinds of thing the Marketplace screen (src/workspace/marketplace-screen.tsx, through src/work-marketplace.mjs) shows on one shelf, in the order they are shown. Each kind says where its rows come from and how a row reads as a shelf item. rows.from is one of the readers the Worker hands in: `store` (a route of the person's own store, the same one their AI calls: method, path, body, and the list inside the reply at `list`, read whole and paged by the Marketplace route) or `page` (a /work/api route of this Worker read with the same session, which pages itself: `query` names the parameters it takes for the search, the offset and the limit, and `total` where its reply says how many there are). fields: for each shelf fact, the paths to try in a row, the first one filled wins. preview: a truthful renderer plus source-row paths; the shared detail view renders the row's actual image, look colours, or layout arrangement. made_by_words: the words the source uses for who made a row, as the person reads them. mine: the paths to a row's fact that says it is the person's own, and the values that mean yes. facts: more labelled facts a card shows, each read from its paths. published.from `pool` names the shared shelf (src/pool.mjs publishedRows) and `shelf` which of its shelves holds this kind; a row this account published there is shown as published. published.from `deploy` (an installable kind with no shelf) means Trillion ships the rows in the deploy (records/starting-set-records.json, src/starting-catalog.mjs), read with no pool read; `deploy: true` on a pool kind (tool, workflow) says Trillion ships some of that kind too, which are looked for in the deploy first. Installable kinds are never shown on the shelf; a Marketplace configuration may hold them (src/marketplace-configurations.mjs). open: the screen a row opens in and the input key its id is given under; null when no screen opens one yet. publish and withdraw: how one of the person's own rows is published or withdrawn: `from` the reader (store or page), the method, the path, and whether its id goes in the body under `id_field` or at the end of the path (`id_in`). A kind that is not published separately (every row of it is already on the shelf) only withdraws. use: what anyone can do with any row of the kind (wear a look), the same route shape with its verb `id`; optional `input_from` maps row values into extra fields required by its owner. verbs: the words each verb shows on a card and a row (label, icon) and says once it is done or has failed; a verb a kind names must have its words here. Adding a kind is a row here, never a change to the screen or the route. link: a web address a row carries to its original (only http and https addresses are shown), with the words and icon the card's button uses. filters: where a self-paging kind's reply lists the fields a person can narrow it by, each field's id, label and choices (a choice is its own words, or { id, label }); a chosen value is sent back to that kind's route as a parameter named by the field's id. rows.query.fixed (optional, `page` kinds): constant parameters the kind always sends with its read, such as which one list of a shared route it shows; a chosen filter or a search never overrides one, so two kinds can share a route and each show only its own list.",
